From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:58:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Find Carla's resources under the prefix on Windows

Carla's plugin UIs are programs in its resources directory, which the
host passes to Carla. On Windows carlabase passes an empty one ("not
yet supported"), so Show GUI has no program to start. Installed in a
prefix, Carla keeps its library in lib/carla and its resources in
share/carla/resources on Windows as on Linux: derive the directory
the same way there.

Upstream: not submitted; master uses <library dir>/resources instead,
the layout of Carla's own Windows installer.
---
 plugins/carlabase/carla.cpp | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/carlabase/carla.cpp b/plugins/carlabase/carla.cpp
index 0029a6b..fe606e2 100644
--- a/plugins/carlabase/carla.cpp
+++ b/plugins/carlabase/carla.cpp
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ CarlaInstrument::CarlaInstrument(InstrumentTrack* const instrumentTrack, const D
     // carla/resources contains PyQt scripts required for launch
     QString dllName(carla_get_library_filename());
     QString resourcesPath;
-#if defined(CARLA_OS_LINUX)
+#if defined(CARLA_OS_LINUX) || defined(CARLA_OS_WIN32) || defined(CARLA_OS_WIN64)
     // parse prefix from dll filename
     QDir path = QFileInfo(dllName).dir();
     path.cdUp();
@@ -153,8 +153,6 @@ CarlaInstrument::CarlaInstrument(InstrumentTrack* const instrumentTrack, const D
     // parse prefix from dll filename
     QDir path = QFileInfo(dllName).dir();
     resourcesPath = path.absolutePath() + "/resources";
-#elif defined(CARLA_OS_WIN32) || defined(CARLA_OS_WIN64)
-    // not yet supported
 #endif
     fHost.resourceDir            = strdup(resourcesPath.toUtf8().constData());
     fHost.get_buffer_size        = host_get_buffer_size;
